{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For from the vine of Sodom is their vine.</b> This is turned back to what precedes — I said in My heart: I will exterminate them and make their memory cease, because their deeds are the deeds of Sodom and Gomorrah." "<b>שדמת.</b> A field of produce, as in ״וּשְׁדֵמוֹת לֹא עָשָׂה אֹכֶל״ (Habakkuk 3), ״בְּשַׁדְמוֹת קִדְרוֹן״ (II Kings 23)." "<b>Bitter grapes.</b> A bitter herb." "<b>Its clusters are bitterness to them.</b> A bitter drink befits them — according to their deeds is their punishment; and so Onkelos renders: ״וְתוּשְׁלָמַת עוֹבָדֵיהוֹן כִּמְרָרוּתְהוֹן״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:27.237100690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}